   1:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c **** /**
   2:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @file
   3:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Transmission Control Protocol for IP
   4:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * See also @ref tcp_raw
   5:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *
   6:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @defgroup tcp_raw TCP
   7:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @ingroup callbackstyle_api
   8:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Transmission Control Protocol for IP\n
   9:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * @see @ref api
  10:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *
  11:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Common functions for the TCP implementation, such as functions
  12:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * for manipulating the data structures and the TCP timer functions. TCP functions
  13:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * related to input and output is found in tcp_in.c and tcp_out.c respectively.\n
  14:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * 
  15:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * TCP connection setup
  16:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * --------------------
  17:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * The functions used for setting up connections is similar to that of
  18:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * the sequential API and of the BSD socket API. A new TCP connection
  19:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * identifier (i.e., a protocol control block - PCB) is created with the
  20:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * tcp_new() function. This PCB can then be either set to listen for new
  21:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * incoming connections or be explicitly connected to another host.
  22:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_new()
  23:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_bind()
  24:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_listen() and tcp_listen_with_backlog()
  25:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_accept()
  26:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_connect()
  27:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * 
  28:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Sending TCP data
  29:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * ----------------
  30:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * TCP data is sent by enqueueing the data with a call to tcp_write() and
  31:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * triggering to send by calling tcp_output(). When the data is successfully
  32:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * transmitted to the remote host, the application will be notified with a
  33:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * call to a specified callback function.
  34:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_write()
  35:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_output()
  36:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_sent()
  37:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * 
  38:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Receiving TCP data
  39:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * ------------------
  40:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * TCP data reception is callback based - an application specified
  41:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * callback function is called when new data arrives. When the
  42:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * application has taken the data, it has to call the tcp_recved()
  43:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * function to indicate that TCP can advertise increase the receive
  44:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * window.
  45:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_recv()
  46:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_recved()
  47:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * 
  48:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Application polling
  49:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * -------------------
  50:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * When a connection is idle (i.e., no data is either transmitted or
  51:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * received), lwIP will repeatedly poll the application by calling a
  52:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * specified callback function. This can be used either as a watchdog
  53:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * timer for killing connections that have stayed idle for too long, or
  54:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * as a method of waiting for memory to become available. For instance,
  55:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * if a call to tcp_write() has failed because memory wasn't available,
  56:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * the application may use the polling functionality to call tcp_write()
  57:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * again when the connection has been idle for a while.
  58:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_poll()
  59:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  *
  60:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * Closing and aborting connections
  61:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * --------------------------------
  62:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_close()
  63:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_abort()
  64:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * - tcp_err()
  65:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  * 
  66:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c ****  */
  67:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp.c **** 
